.TH mnnn-org 1  "mnnn-org 2.13.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-org \- Organizations: members with roles, shared resources and projects, rules and code answering requests, and an HTTPS site (HTML, JSON, gRPC) for what you publish
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn org\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Organizations: members with roles, shared resources and projects, rules and code answering requests, and an HTTPS site (HTML, JSON, gRPC) for what you publish
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Orgs you create here are run by this node, and you are their owner. Orgs on other nodes
are joined by applying (an owner or admin approves) or by answering an invitation; both
are key exchanges scoped to the org. Commands that take ORG act on an org of yours, or
on a joined org through its node when you have the permission there.
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn org create "Comet Lab" \-\-public
  mnnn org member invite comet\-lab \-\-peer ben \-\-role user
  mnnn org apply /ip4/10.0.0.2/tcp/4741/p2p/12D3Koo… comet\-lab \-\-note "hi"
  mnnn org member approve comet\-lab cleo \-\-role viewer
  mnnn org resource add comet\-lab journal "field notes"
  mnnn org publish comet\-lab "field notes" \-\-to public
  mnnn org edit comet\-lab \-\-hosted on && mnnn org host start
  mnnn org cert acme \-\-domain lab.example.org \-\-email me@example.org
.PP
See `mnnn help organizations` and `mnnn help org\-hosting`.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-org\-create(1)
Create an organization (private, members only, until you say otherwise)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-edit(1)
Change an organization
.TP
mnnn\-org\-remove(1)
Delete an organization of yours (its resources stay here as they are)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-list(1)
Your organizations and the ones you joined
.TP
mnnn\-org\-show(1)
One organization: settings, roles, members, resources, projects, endpoints
.TP
mnnn\-org\-role(1)
Roles and their permissions
.TP
mnnn\-org\-member(1)
Members: applications, invitations, roles and kicks
.TP
mnnn\-org\-resource(1)
What an org holds (given to it, or added here)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-publish(1)
Put a resource on the org\*(Aqs site
.TP
mnnn\-org\-unpublish(1)
Take a resource off the org\*(Aqs site
.TP
mnnn\-org\-project(1)
Projects of the org and their members
.TP
mnnn\-org\-endpoint(1)
Rules, code spaces and models that answer requests
.TP
mnnn\-org\-code(1)
The org\*(Aqs code spaces this node runs (each node chooses its own)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-call(1)
Call an endpoint (of your org, or of a joined org through its node)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-template(1)
Site templates and their assets
.TP
mnnn\-org\-browse(1)
The organizations a node lists (public ones), or one by slug or id
.TP
mnnn\-org\-apply(1)
Apply to an organization on another node
.TP
mnnn\-org\-join(1)
Accept an invitation: the invite link, or the org name of one sent to this node (`\-` reads stdin)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-sync(1)
Check a joined org: an answer to your application, your role and permissions
.TP
mnnn\-org\-leave(1)
Leave a joined org
.TP
mnnn\-org\-fetch(1)
Fetch a resource of a joined org
.TP
mnnn\-org\-give(1)
Give one of your things to a joined org (a copy, owned by the org)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-mirror(1)
Copy a joined org\*(Aqs public site here to serve it (needs the host permission)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-sync\-code(1)
Copy a joined org\*(Aqs code spaces here to run them (needs host and code.view); changed ones ask for approval again
.TP
mnnn\-org\-sign(1)
The `Authorization` header for a signed web request to a joined org\*(Aqs site
.TP
mnnn\-org\-sign\-in(1)
A one\-time browser sign\-in link to a joined org\*(Aqs site (valid five minutes, once)
.TP
mnnn\-org\-host(1)
Serve hosted orgs over HTTPS
.TP
mnnn\-org\-cert(1)
The site\*(Aqs TLS certificate (self\-signed, or ACME / Let\*(Aqs Encrypt)
